<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patrick Tonyn</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1725–1804</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patrick Tonyn was a British army officer who was governor of the Province of East <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/florida">Florida</a> from 1774 to 1785. During the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/american-revolutionary-war">American Revolutionary War</a> he made the colony a refuge for loyalists and a base for raids into <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/georgia">Georgia</a>. He oversaw the British evacuation after the colony was returned to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a> in 1783.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patrick-tonyn.jpg" alt="Patrick Tonyn" width="320" height="354" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: George Clint · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patrick_Tonyn.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
